// pfodWeb NOTE: this board only exists in the real Arduino IDE as a
// "Revision" submenu option under a different parent board id (no
// standalone <id>.name= boards.txt entry of its own), so the normal
// boards.txt id lookup can't give it a unique name — without this
// override it would silently collide with every other board sharing
// this chip's default boardName. Full copy of variants/esp32/esp32/board.json with
// only boardName/displayName changed.
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO25 tagged "led_high" - confirmed onboard green status LED (active-high) via official Zephyr board devicetree (zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr boards/lilygo/ttgo_lora32: "led_0 { gpios = <&gpio0 25 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>; label = \"Green - LED0\"; }"), corroborated by official LilyGO schematic Xinyuan-LilyGO/LilyGo-LoRa-Series T3_V1.6.1.pdf (GREEN LED wired to IO25) and wiki.lilygo.cc T3 pin table ("Onboard LED" = GPIO25). GPIO0 (pins_arduino.h KEY_BUILTIN alias) was investigated but NOT tagged as a button - the same official schematic shows no pushbutton wired to GPIO0 (only a RESET button on RST/EN and a power slide switch); see boardsDetails notes.txt for full detail.
